# Catalog Ontology Naming

`catalog/extras/sysmlv2-ontology/MAPPING.md` is the **naming authority** for catalog types vs SysML v2 / KerML concepts. When a rule, doc, or export name disagrees with Rust source, trust `catalog/src` and reconcile prose against `MAPPING.md`.

Current vocabulary (post P0-P3; wire-format names in committed JSON may still differ -- see `WIRE_SURFACE.md`):

| Rust type | Replaces (historical) |
|---|---|
| `UseCase` | `UserJourney` |
| `Connection` | `Edge` |
| `TcpPort` | `Port(u16)` |
| `PortKind` | `Interface` enum |
| `Action`, `ActionId`, `ActionCatalog` | `Function`, `FunctionId`, `FunctionCatalog` |
| `ServiceJudgment` | `ServiceDefinition` |
| `RequirementClass` | `RequirementKind` |
| `Assumption` on `Requirement` | `RequirementKind::Constraint` |
| `Availability` | `FeatureAvailability` |
| `IntroTraces` | `FeatureTraces` |
| `CapabilityId` | requirement subject (deleted `Feature` types) |
| `VerificationRecord`, `Verdict` | harness step / journey outcomes |

Frozen by wire format: `JourneyId` variant names (see `WIRE_SURFACE.md`). `Action` has no I/O fields or child actions.

Rework plan and phase status: `catalog/extras/sysmlv2-ontology/PLAN.md`.
